[ar:Slim Dusty]
[al:The Very Best Of Slim Dusty]
[ti:By A Fire Of Gidgee Coal]
[00:10.46] By a warm electric heater and a softly padded chair
[00:17.47] In a lounge room brightly lighted by a glowing chandelier
[00:24.21] Since my early days of drovin' the years have taken toll
[00:33.18] But I somehow miss my swag wrap by a fire of Gidgee coal
[00:42.65] When I wake from sleep each morning and I ring the bedside bell
[00:51.31] The maid brings in my breakfast and she fills my pipe as well
[01:00.63] There are cakes and sweetened coffee on a tray of sparkling gold
[01:07.52] But I miss black tea and damper by a fire of Gidgee coal
[01:32.47] I am driven' out each evening by a chauffeur spruce and neat
[01:42.39] Through the flowered parks and gardens and the crowded city streets
[01:50.69] But I drift back through the ages while the big car softly rolls
[01:57.99] To a stock route and a wagonette and a fire of Gidgee coal
[02:09.92] I attend all social parties in the rich parts of the town
[02:16.63] Drinking wine from fancy glasses as the waiters go their rounds
[02:25.58] But I'd rather share a bottle with those drovin' mates of old
[02:32.96] In a pair of dusty moleskins by a fire of Gidgee coal
[02:42.14] In a pair of dusty moleskins by a fire of Gidgee coal
[02:54.00] 
